     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks like it may be an error.\n\n**The problem:** Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to **6400 mg/day**.\n- The usual maximum single dose is **800 mg**. 1600 mg is twice that.\n- The usual maximum daily dose for prescription use is **3200 mg/day**. This order is twice that.\n- Doses this high raise the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and other NSAID toxicity, especially in a 70-year-old... I mean, in any adult. Even with normal kidney and liver function, this is well outside the labeled range.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **400 mg four times daily** (1600 mg/day total). This is a common analgesic regimen and may be what \"1600\" referred to.\n2. **800 mg four times daily** (3200 mg/day). This is the maximum labeled daily dose.\n3. **Something else**, such as a different drug or frequency.\n\nTell me which one you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do mean 1600 mg four times daily for a specific clinical reason, please confirm that and give a brief rationale. I'll add it to the order note so pharmacy can see it when they verify the order."
      }
     ],
